            "result_text": "I'll help you set up a git server with automatic deployment to a web server. Here's the complete setup:\n\n## Server Setup (on your server machine)\n\n### 1. Create a bare git repository\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p /git/server\ncd /git/server\ngit init --bare\n```\n\n### 2. Create the deployment directory\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p /var/www/html\n```\n\n### 3. Set up the git post-receive hook\n\nCreate `/git/server/hooks/post-receive` with the following content:\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nGIT_WORK_TREE=/var/www/html git checkout -f\n```\n\nMake it executable:\n```bash\nchmod +x /git/server/hooks/post-receive\n```\n\n### 4. Start a web server on port 8080\n\nUse a simple Python HTTP server or Node.js. Here's Python:\n\n```bash\ncd /var/www/html\npython3 -m http.server 8080\n```\n\nOr if you prefer something persistent, install and run nginx or Apache. For a quick test, you can also use:\n\n```bash\ncd /var/www/html\nnpx http-server -p 8080\n```\n\n## Client Usage (on your local machine)\n\nOnce SSH login is configured, you can then:\n\n```bash\ngit clone user@server:/git/server myrepo\ncd myrepo\necho \"hello world\" > hello.html\ngit add hello.html\ngit commit -m \"add hello.html\"\ngit push origin master\n```\n\nThen verify:\n```bash\ncurl http://server:8080/hello.html\n```\n\n## How it works\n\n- The bare git repository (`/git/server`) receives pushes\n- The `post-receive` hook automatically checks out the latest code to `/var/www/html`\n- The web server serves files from `/var/www/html` on port 8080\n\nThat's it! The post-receive hook makes deployment automatic—every push deploys instantly."
